{"version": 2, "width": 100, "height": 40, "timestamp": 1785763398, "idle_time_limit": 3.0, "env": {"SHELL": "/bin/bash", "TERM": "xterm-256color"}, "title": "h5explain: options, offset jumps, header messages, B-tree traversal, and policy"}
[0.004781, "o", "\u001b[?2004hh5pickles$ "]
[0.64147, "o", "./tools/h5explain --help"]
[0.641924, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[0.657025, "o", "Usage:\r\n"]
[0.657226, "o", "  h5explain [OPTIONS] FILE [OFFSET]\r\n  h5explain -h|--help\r\n\r\nArguments:\r\n  FILE       HDF5 file to open with GNU poke\r\n  OFFSET     Optional starting byte offset, decimal or hexadecimal (0x...)\r\n\r\nOptions:\r\n  -h, --help           show this help\r\n  -n, --non-strict     use non-strict poke mapping to keep exploring\r\n  -c, --command CMD    run CMD after startup; may be repeated\r\n  -b, --batch          run commands and exit instead of entering the REPL\r\n  -q, --quiet          suppress the startup banner\r\n      --policy         load the h5policy pickles (check, check_all, profile)\r\n      --no-policy      do not load them, even if the commands look like they need them\r\n\r\nThe policy pickles roughly double startup, so they load only when the session\r\nmay use them: always when interactive, and in batch only when the commands\r\nmention a policy command.  Use --policy if a batch session reaches check\r\nindirectly, or --no-policy to keep a scripted sweep as fast as possible.\r\n\r\nCommands come from --command options, or, when none are given and standard\r\ninput is not a terminal, from standard input.  Either source implies --batch\r\nand --quiet, so a scripted session works without extra flags:\r\n\r\n  printf 'root\\nls\\n' | h5explain examples/file.h5\r\n  h5explain -c root -c ls examples/file.h5\r\n\r\nBatch mode exits with poke's status.  Note that poke reports an unhandled\r\nexception on stderr and continues, so scripted callers should assert on\r\noutput rather than on the exit status alone.\r\n"]
[0.6575, "o", "\u001b[?2004hh5pickles$ "]
[3.445301, "o", "clear\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[3.446945, "o", "\u001b[H\u001b[2J\u001b[3J"]
[3.447155, "o", "\u001b[?2004hh5pickles$ "]
[4.047601, "o", "./tools/h5explain -q --no-policy examples/file.h5\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[4.533804, "o", "current: HDF5 superblock at 0UL#B [superblock]\r\n(h5explain) \u001b[?2004h"]
[5.250226, "o", "root\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
