[8.544098, "o", "[context] v1 raw chunk B-tree ndims set to 3UB from layout message\r\ncurrent: object header at 195UL#B\r\n(h5explain) "]
[8.544283, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[9.260232, "o", "pwd\r\n"]
[9.260267, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[9.260499, "o", "(unlabeled) at 195UL#B (object header)\r\n"]
[9.260597, "o", "(h5explain) "]
[9.260613, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[10.062286, "o", "explain_msg (4)\r\n"]
[10.062357, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[10.091065, "o", "Object-header message 4: Data layout (type=0x0000000000000008)\r\n  prefix_offset=297UL#B\r\n  payload_offset=301UL#B\r\n  payload_size=23\r\n  flags=0UB\r\n\r\nWhat it is:\r\n  The data-layout message says where an object's raw data is stored and\r\n  which storage scheme is used.\r\n\r\nKey fields:\r\n  version=3UB\r\n  layout_class=2UB (chunked)\r\n  ndims=3UB\r\n  chunk_index_addr=479UL#B\r\n  stored_element_size=4\r\n\r\nWhy it matters:\r\n  The layout determines whether data bytes are inline, contiguous,\r\n  chunk-indexed, or virtual. Chunked layouts point at the metadata\r\n  structures that h5explain can traverse.\r\n"]
[10.091329, "o", "(h5explain) "]
[10.091342, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[11.666743, "o", "check\r\n"]
[11.666808, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[11.701258, "o", "h5policy: accept_with_warnings (profile untrusted_strict)\r\n"]
[11.70363, "o", "Findings bearing on the current primitive (195UL#B):\r\n  @0x000000000000011f warning H5_ADVISORY_DECODE_FILTER  [/DirectChunkData]\r\n    dataset declares the deflate/gzip filter; a consumer must decode/decompress untrusted data to read it\r\n"]
[11.703927, "o", "(h5explain) \u001b[?2004h"]
